<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
  <!ENTITY name "md12xx.fancontrol">
  <!ENTITY author "TheIlluminate92">
  <!ENTITY version "@@PLUGIN_VERSION@@">
  <!ENTITY launch "MD12xxFanControl">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;" pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TheIlluminate92/unraid-md12xx-fan-control/main/releases/md12xx.fancontrol.plg" min="7.3.2" support="https://forums.unraid.net/topic/200454-plugin-md12xx-fan-control-dell-md1200-md1220-fan-control-beta/" icon="icon.png">
<CHANGES>
### 0.5.0 Beta - Build 2026.10.22.04
- Adds configurable downshift hysteresis to each Individual shelf/IPMI curve; Global devices follow the Global hysteresis. IPMI defaults to 1°C, increases speed immediately, and delays downshifts until below the threshold minus hysteresis. Fault/thermal handback remains immediate.
- Individual IPMI curves now support a 15% minimum. Global and MD12xx shelf curves retain their 20% minimum. Emergency iDRAC cooling takes priority over a curve's maximum.
- Adds disabled-by-default local IPMI chassis control for R730/R730xd, with a bundled static tool and licenses. Thermal or sensor faults return control to iDRAC; persistent host-bound ownership supports recovery after process loss or reboot. Live R730xd fan response and explicit firmware handback passed; load, 15% hardware response, crash recovery and reboot validation remain pending.
- Each shelf and IPMI may follow the Global curve or retain an Individual curve. Each device uses its own temperature; mixed Global/Individual setups are supported.
- Hides unavailable hardware sections, with a Show unavailable controls option. Adds the bundled plugin PNG icon and preserves the existing update identity and MD12xx commissioning.

### 0.4.14 - Build 2026.10.20.01
- Partial active-temperature loss and failed/missing fans now fail safe in Auto. Commissioning monitors thermal demand and preserves higher cooling on abort. Status-aware supervision and staged runtime validation/rollback preserve saved commissioning. Adds safety/activation regressions and migration documentation. New failure paths are software-tested; supervised hardware validation remains pending.

### 0.4.13 - Build 2026.10.12.01
- Rejects noncanonical installer filenames and duplicate internal-name registrations before touching runtime or configuration.
- Keeps canonical install/update naming, date-based build metadata, and existing project credits.
- Registration migration requires a reviewed backup and cleanup; no automatic removal or hardware changes.

### 0.4.12 - Build 2026.10.11.01
- Fixes normal update detection from test builds and older semantic versions by using date-based Unraid package versioning.
- Keeps application version 0.4.12 in Settings/API while Installed Plugins shows the update build number.
- Preserves the 0.4.11 identity tracking and guarded startup recovery behavior; no hardware settings or calibration migration changes.

### 0.4.11
- Tracks each commissioned shelf by persistent enclosure identity across reboot, device renumbering, and host moves.
- Fixes stale-address commissioning filters and rejects disk targets masquerading as SES enclosures.
- Adds selectable, once-per-boot 35% startup recovery for already RPM-commissioned, cool shelves at a proven 20% baseline.
- Requires healthy fan telemetry, unique response, the same saved identity/disks, and verified restoration; increased cooling demand aborts recovery without lowering required cooling.
- Bounds recovery, pauses normal writes, serializes test launches, and preserves commissioned identities/calibration.
- Consolidates disk parsing and response/restoration logic, corrects capture labels, redacts saved identities, and normalizes installer checksums.
- Upgrade: legacy address-only shelves require one supervised Identify &amp; test; successful test2 commissioning remains valid.
- Automated checks passed. Top-shelf commissioning/restoration passed on hardware. Conditional 35% startup recovery remains unexercised on hardware and is released at the owner's request.

### 0.4.10 Beta
- Matches a serial EMM's reported ELI address to the SES enclosure logical identifier when independent SES RPM proof fails.
- Keeps RPM-verified commissioning where it works; SAS-matched shelves show reduced fan-response verification.

### 0.4.9 Beta
- Adds a guarded manual shelf ramp and explicit operator-confirmed serial-to-SES pairing when SES fan RPM remains static.
- Keeps operator-confirmed shelves visibly unverified by RPM; serial command acknowledgements and disk-temperature fail-safe control remain active.
- Includes an opt-in EMM console inventory for `_who`, `_ver`, and the command listing, plus read-only SES and inquiry captures.

### 0.4.8 Beta
- Records a 30-second 20% baseline, then samples 50% SES telemetry every five seconds until one unique response is stable within 10% across two readings or a 60-second safety timeout is reached.
- Keeps timed 20% and 50% sample histories in the downloadable commissioning results for troubleshooting slower firmware telemetry.

### 0.4.7 Beta
- Rejects malformed or traversing serial adapter paths before any hardware access.
- Uses method-specific request parsing in the WebGUI API and adds security regression coverage.
- Uses the public Unraid support thread in release and Community Apps metadata.

### 0.4.6 Beta
- Shows the friendly MD12xx Fan Control name and description on Unraid's Plugins page without changing the internal package ID.
- Verifies that the Plugins-page display metadata remains in every built installer.

### 0.4.5 Beta
- Uses Unraid's supported stock server icon on the Plugins page.
- Restores the GitHub issue forms with native attachment-capable diagnostic text areas.
- Records a successful overnight Auto-mode soak on the two-shelf MD1200 test system.

### 0.4.4 Beta
- Clarifies the tested service cable, FTDI adapter, HBA/SES path, model boundaries, and commissioning recovery steps.
- States explicitly that HBA access is read-only and fan commands travel only through the selected USB serial console.
- Adds concrete Community Apps requirements and private security-reporting enablement guidance.

### 0.4.3 Beta
- Supervises the fan controller, restarts unexpected exits with bounded backoff, and raises local Unraid failure/recovery notifications.
- Exposes watchdog state in Settings and redacted local diagnostics.
- Documents hardware prerequisites, adds Community Apps screenshots, and sets the tested minimum to Unraid 7.3.2.
- Adds a privacy-first support flow: export diagnostics locally, review them, then open a public GitHub issue and attach them manually.
- Adds optional diagnostic archive upload fields and mandatory privacy confirmations to the GitHub issue forms.
- Documents AI-assisted development roles in Settings, project documentation, and Community Apps metadata.

### 0.4.2 Beta
- Disables serial adapters already selected by another shelf immediately, without a page refresh.

### 0.4.1 Beta
- Uses Unraid's stock Disk Settings icon metadata for a reliable Settings tile across themes.
- Makes the Auto curve point count resize after typing or changing the requested count.
- Makes Refresh discovery save only discovery options and run one guarded pass immediately.
- Shows controller fault details, target reasons, telemetry state, and command state in the app.
- Prevents duplicate hardware assignments and blocks configuration or control writes during Identify &amp; test.
- Stops tests safely during update/uninstall and avoids rebuilding the form from completed jobs.
- Fixes archive downloads, strengthens diagnostic redaction, and hardens inline configuration encoding.
- Saves commissioning RPM calibration, verifies later commands against SES telemetry, and detects response drift.
- Uses fail-safe speed for incomplete or changed disk mappings and recovers stale commissioning locks.
- Keeps Settings open while downloading local diagnostic and test archives.

### 0.4.0 Beta
- Adds fully app-driven Identify &amp; test with live progress and safe server-side continuation.
- Adds a packaged Settings icon and fixes shelf-name editing so refreshes do not steal focus.
- Uses generic competing-controller messages and reports blocked shelf writes accurately.
- Lowers hardware telemetry polling to 5 seconds while saved control changes remain immediate.
- Removes installation-specific wording from the public interface and documentation.

### 0.3.0 Beta
- Adds Manual speeds from 20% through 100% in 10% increments.
- Turns off active FTDI testing automatically after setup; passive inventory remains available.
- Makes uninstall a complete reset that removes persistent configuration and commissioning results.
- Adds expandable setup help, clearer disk mappings, a 2–10 point stacked Auto curve, and local redacted diagnostics.
- Adds Community Apps metadata, hardware-report forms, privacy/security documentation, and generic MD1220 test coverage.
- MD1200 is hardware-tested; MD1220 and additional HBA/firmware reports are requested.

### 0.2.3
- Uses the hardware-proven reader-first serial session for every speed command.
- Requires independent SES RPM proof of the final 20% restoration before commissioning succeeds.

### 0.2.2
- Maps disks through the verified SES device's SAS expander when enclosure-class links are unavailable.
- Prevents discovery from racing the commissioning test's final 20% safety restore.

### 0.2.1
- Fixes BlueDress speed writes by keeping the serial console open read/write and consuming its replies.

### 0.2.0
- Adds RPM-proven automatic serial-to-SES identification and automatic Unraid disk assignment.
- Keeps a manual mapping fallback and refuses ambiguous or empty automatic mappings.

### 0.1.3
- Fixes the blank Unraid Settings page caused by page-builder path resolution.

### 0.1.2
- Moves updates and support to the dedicated standalone repository.

### 0.1.1
- Validates conservative discovery against mixed USB serial and SES hardware.
- Fixes the controller startup parser and adds an installation banner.

### 0.1.0
- Initial standalone beta for Dell PowerVault MD1200 and MD1220 shelves.
- Adds multi-shelf configuration, conservative background discovery, Auto/Manual control, independent RPM telemetry, locking, and guarded commissioning.
- Optional serial verification is read-only, requires an MD12xx-shaped `_who` response, and is blocked while another fan controller is active.
</CHANGES>

<!-- Unraid names inline scripts after the installer basename. Reject aliases before touching runtime/config. -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
set -e
case "${0##*/}" in
  inline1-md12xx.fancontrol.sh) ;;
  *)
    echo "Refusing a noncanonical installer filename. Save/install this package as md12xx.fancontrol.plg."
    echo "Do not uninstall an alias registration: it may share configuration with the canonical plugin."
    exit 1
    ;;
esac
php <<'PLUGIN_REGISTRATION_CHECK'
<?php
$canonical = 'md12xx.fancontrol.plg';
foreach (['/boot/config/plugins', '/var/log/plugins'] as $directory) {
    foreach (glob($directory . '/*.plg') ?: [] as $path) {
        if (basename($path) === $canonical) continue;
        libxml_use_internal_errors(true);
        $manifest = @simplexml_load_file($path, 'SimpleXMLElement', LIBXML_NONET);
        if ($manifest !== false && (string)$manifest['name'] === 'md12xx.fancontrol') {
            file_put_contents('php://stderr', "Duplicate plugin registration: " . basename($path) . "\n");
            file_put_contents('php://stderr', "Back up shared data and migrate the registration before updating. Do not use Uninstall.\n");
            exit(1);
        }
    }
}
PLUGIN_REGISTRATION_CHECK
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
set -e
RUNTIME_DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol"
CONFIG_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol"

# Populate a separate tree while the installed runtime keeps running.
[ ! -L "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/.md12xx.fancontrol.staged" ] || { echo "Staging path is a symlink" >&2; exit 1; }
rm -rf -- "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/.md12xx.fancontrol.staged"
mkdir -p "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/.md12xx.fancontrol.staged" "$CONFIG_DIR"
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

@@FILES@@

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
set -e
RUNTIME_DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/.md12xx.fancontrol.staged"
CONFIG_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol"
CONFIG_FILE="$CONFIG_DIR/config.json"

chmod 0644 "$RUNTIME_DIR/MD12xxFanControl.page" "$RUNTIME_DIR/icon.svg" "$RUNTIME_DIR/assets/css/settings.css" "$RUNTIME_DIR/assets/js/settings.js" "$RUNTIME_DIR/assets/icon.svg"
chmod 0644 "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/common.php" "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/controller.php" "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/discovery.php" "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/api.php" "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/download.php" "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/quiet.php" "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/safety.php" "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/commission-safety.php" "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/watchdog-health.php"
chmod 0644 "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stable-response.awk" "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/select-candidates.awk"
chmod 0755 "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/start.sh" "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh" "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/controller-supervisor.sh" "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/diagnose.sh" "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/interrogate-emm.sh" "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/commission.sh" "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/commission-job.sh"
chmod 0755 "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/ipmi-supervisor.sh" "$RUNTIME_DIR/bin/ipmitool.bin"
chmod 0644 "$RUNTIME_DIR/icon.png"
php -r '$image = getimagesize($argv[1]); if (!$image || $image[0] !== 256 || $image[1] !== 256 || $image[2] !== IMAGETYPE_PNG) exit(1);' "$RUNTIME_DIR/icon.png"
"$RUNTIME_DIR/bin/ipmitool.bin" -V >/dev/null
(cd "$RUNTIME_DIR/bin" && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS >/dev/null)

for PHP_FILE in "$RUNTIME_DIR"/include/*.php; do php -l "$PHP_FILE" >/dev/null; done

for SHELL_FILE in "$RUNTIME_DIR"/scripts/*.sh; do bash -n "$SHELL_FILE"; done

# Staged validation must complete before stopping the installed processes.
STAGED_DIR="$RUNTIME_DIR"
RUNTIME_DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol"
PREVIOUS_DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/.md12xx.fancontrol.previous"
[ ! -L "$RUNTIME_DIR" ] && [ ! -L "$PREVIOUS_DIR" ] || exit 1
HAD_PREVIOUS=false
ACTIVATING=false
rollback_runtime() {
  local result=$?
  if [ "$result" -ne 0 ] && [ "$ACTIVATING" = true ]; then
    # A failed new start must be stopped before a previous writer is restored.
    if [ -x "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh" ] && ! "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh"; then
      echo "New runtime could not stop; previous runtime retained for supervised recovery." >&2
      return
    fi
    rm -rf -- "$RUNTIME_DIR"
    if $HAD_PREVIOUS; then
      mv -- "$PREVIOUS_DIR" "$RUNTIME_DIR"
      "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/start.sh" || true
    fi
    echo "Plugin activation failed; prior runtime restored when available." >&2
  fi
}
trap rollback_runtime EXIT
if [ -x "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh" ]; then "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh"; fi
# Keep a previous successful runtime until the next activation. Never touch config.
if [ -d "$RUNTIME_DIR" ]; then
  rm -rf -- "$PREVIOUS_DIR"
  mv -- "$RUNTIME_DIR" "$PREVIOUS_DIR"
  HAD_PREVIOUS=true
fi
ACTIVATING=true
mv -- "$STAGED_DIR" "$RUNTIME_DIR"

if [ ! -f "$CONFIG_FILE" ]; then
  cat > "$CONFIG_FILE" <<'MD12XX_CONFIG'
{
  "enabled": false,
  "mode": "auto",
  "manualSpeed": 20,
  "pollSeconds": 5,
  "reassertSeconds": 900,
  "sensorFailureSpeed": 50,
  "hysteresisC": 1,
  "discovery": {
    "autoProbeKnownFtdi": false,
    "intervalSeconds": 300,
    "responseSeconds": 3
  },
  "curve": [
    {"temperatureC": 0, "speed": 20},
    {"temperatureC": 35, "speed": 25},
    {"temperatureC": 45, "speed": 30},
    {"temperatureC": 50, "speed": 50}
  ],
  "legacyContainerNames": ["MD1200-Fan-Controller"],
  "shelves": []
}
MD12XX_CONFIG
fi

chmod 0644 "$CONFIG_FILE"
php -r '
  require $argv[1];
  $config = md12xx_read_config($argv[2]);
  $updated = md12xx_disable_active_discovery_after_setup($config);
  if (($config["discovery"]["autoProbeKnownFtdi"] ?? false) && !($updated["discovery"]["autoProbeKnownFtdi"] ?? false)) {
    md12xx_write_config($updated, $argv[2]);
    echo "Setup is already complete; active connection testing was turned off.\n";
  }
' "$RUNTIME_DIR/include/common.php" "$CONFIG_FILE"
mkdir -p /var/run/md12xx.fancontrol
"$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/start.sh"
trap - EXIT
cat <<'MD12XX_BANNER'

              \   |   /
            ---\  |  /---
          -------(O)-------
            ---/  |  \---
              /   |   \

             MD12xx FAN CONTROL
      Storage is awesome. Quiet is power.

MD12XX_BANNER
echo "Version @@VERSION@@ installed. Configure it under Settings → Utilities."
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
set -e
RUNTIME_DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol"
CONFIG_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol"
if [ -x "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh" ]; then
  "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh"
fi
rm -rf "$RUNTIME_DIR" "/var/run/md12xx.fancontrol" "$CONFIG_DIR"
rm -rf "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/.md12xx.fancontrol.staged" "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/.md12xx.fancontrol.previous"
rm -f "/boot/config/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol.plg"
echo "MD12xx Fan Control removed. Configuration, commissioning results, and runtime state were deleted."
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>
</PLUGIN>
